### The Test Cabinet ###

# Ignore cspell's autogenerated cache file
.cspellcache

# Rendered reference screenshots are a build output: the harness renders each
# HTML mockup to a screenshot under the case's `reference/.rendered/` cache (see
# crates/core/src/reference.rs). That cache is regenerated and must never be
# committed — for ANY case, any type/difficulty/slug/version.
test-cases/**/reference/.rendered/

# `reference/screenshots/`, by contrast, is NOT ignored: it holds the *committed*
# media screenshots a `media`-based case serves as-is (captured from its playable
# reference-impl — the source of truth, since it has no mockup to render). Because
# the rendered cache lives elsewhere, these can be tracked wholesale with no
# per-case enumeration, so a new media-based case's screenshots are committed
# automatically.

# Cargo build output. Cargo.lock is intentionally committed because this
# workspace builds applications (the CLI and desktop app), not just libraries.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Ignore the output of test runs. Anchored to the repository root: `tcab` writes
# runs to ./runs (see `--out-dir`), but an unanchored `runs/` also matches source
# directories such as apps/site/src/pages/runs/, silently excluding real code.
/runs/

# Scratch output for inspecting seeded run inputs (`tcab seed`). This is local
# inspection material, not something that should be committed.
tmp/

# Ignore generated workflows
.claude/workflows/

# Ignore Sqlite files used by services
tcab-auth.sqlite*
tcab-backend.sqlite*

# The backend's on-disk definition store (default TCAB_BACKEND_STORE=./tcab-store).
# Generated by ingest from the checkout — local state, not source. Anchored to the
# repo root so it can't match a nested source directory of the same name.
/tcab-store/

# Ignore driver-generated run scratch + the local artifact-service store
/.tcab-driver/
/tcab-artifacts/

# `tcab validate --implementation <dir>` writes synthesized validation media into a
# `.tcab/` folder inside the target build directory (e.g. a case's reference-impl).
# It is transient output, regenerated on demand — never source. Not anchored, so it
# matches the folder at any depth.
.tcab/

# scripts/reingest.sh change-detection baseline (its mtime = last successful
# re-ingest). Per-checkout local state, not source. Anchored to the repo root.
/.reingest-timestamp

# Claude memories — host-mounted for container-rebuild persistence, not committed
.claude/memories/

# Python bytecode caches (e.g. from the Blender container's helper modules being
# imported during local development — see containers/blender/). Never source.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
